WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.730
As Ginni Bazlinton reached Antarctica, she found herself greeted by a group of little Gentoo penguins longing to say hello.
金妮·巴兹林顿抵达南极洲时，迎接她的是一群急着跟她打招呼的小巴布亚企鹅。

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:15.990
These gentle, lovely gatekeepers welcomed her and kick-started what was to be a trip Ginni would never forget.
这些温顺可爱的“守门人”迎接了她，也由此开启了一段注定让金妮终生难忘的旅程。

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:21.860
Ever since her childhood, Ginni, now 71, has had a deep love for travel.
金妮如今71岁，从童年起就一直深爱旅行。

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:28.840
Throughout her career as a professional dancer, she toured in the UK, but always longed to explore further.
在整个职业舞蹈演员生涯中，她一直在英国各地巡演，但始终渴望去更远的地方探索。

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.960
When she retired from dancing and her sons eventually flew the nest, she decided it was time to take the plunge.
等她告别舞台、儿子们也终于离家独立后，她认定是时候勇敢迈出这一步了。

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:45.950
After taking a degree at Chichester University in Related Arts, Ginni began to travel the world, eventually getting work teaching English in Japan and Chile.
在奇切斯特大学获得相关艺术专业学位后，金妮开始周游世界，后来在日本和智利找到了教英语的工作。

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:57.000
And it was in Chile she discovered she could get last-minute cheap deals on ships going to Antarctica from the islands off Tierra del Fuego, the southernmost tip of South America.
也正是在智利，她发现，从南美洲最南端火地岛附近的岛屿开往南极洲的船，临近开船时能买到便宜的特价票。

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.990
“I just decided I wanted to go,” she says.
“我就是打定主意要去，”她说。

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:05.680
“I had no idea about what I’d find there and I wasn’t nervous, I just wanted to do it.
“我完全不知道会在那里看到什么，也不紧张，我就是想去做这件事。

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.760
And I wanted to do it alone as I always prefer it that way.”
而且我想独自去，因为我一向更喜欢那样。”

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:18.360
In March 2008, Ginni boarded a ship with 48 passengers she’d never met before, to begin the journey towards Antarctica.
2008年3月，金妮和48位素不相识的乘客一起登上一艘船，开始了前往南极洲的旅程。

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.930
“From seeing the wildlife to witnessing sunrises, the whole experience was amazing.
“从观赏野生动物到亲眼看日出，整个经历都太棒了。

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:28.860
Antarctica left an impression on me that no other place has,” Ginni says.
南极洲给我留下的印象，是别的任何地方都不曾给过我的，”金妮说。

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:37.452
“I remember the first time I saw a humpback whale; it just rose out of the water like some prehistoric creature and I thought it was smiling at us.
“我记得第一次看到座头鲸的情景；它就那样从水里浮了上来，像某种史前生物，我觉得它在对我们微笑。

00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:41.702
You could still hear the operatic sounds it was making underwater.”
你还能听到它在水下发出的歌剧般的声音。”

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:49.442
The realization that this is a precious land, to be respected by humans, was one of the biggest things that hit home to Ginni.
意识到这是一片珍贵的土地，应当受到人类的尊重——这是让金妮感触最深的事情之一。
